e hard coking coal (“",{"type":"b","children":["MV HCC"]},"”) sold by the Group through auctions on the Mongolian Stock Exchange (“",{"type":"b","children":["MSE"]},"”) commodity exchange platform under delivery-at-place Ganqimaodu (“",{"type":"b","children":["DAP GM"]},"”) terms during the period from 1 January to 30 September 2026 are shown in Chart 1 below (publicly available source: ",{"type":"url","params":{"url":"https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=vSZ-tlneXmI2v6HctVoqppf4riaMt-3R0FKfDNd2FriZeiRMeoaDQ5kRiVJuo-Fy4jz53vVPW8sxfqDoGPtgZ127SHMCrrzM9lZAEQi8hAs=","linkText":"https://www.mse.mn/trade"}},")."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Chart 1. MSE auction prices for MV HCC from 1 January to 30 September 2026:"]}]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":[{"type":"news-image","params":{"image":{"id":"globenewswire:52d75f6c2094b-f6d5d05c8367f450919137049c71c767","alt":"MSE auction prices for MV HCC from 1 January to 30 September 2026","source-width":1188,"source-height":370,"bg-color":"#fbfbfb"}}}]}]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"i","children":["Note: Each dot represents individual batch of 12,800 tonnes of MV HCC successfully auctioned via MSE commodity exchange trading platform, with prices shown in RMB per tonne under DAP GM terms, exclusive of the applicable 3% import duty and 13% VAT in the PRC."]}]},{"type":"p","children":["During the quarter ended 30 September 2026, the number of coal-loaded trucks crossing the border to GM decreased to an average of 897 trucks per operating day, 34% and 29% lower than the averages of 1,366 and 1,270 trucks per operating day for the quarters ended 30 June 2026 and 31 March 2026, respectively. Nevertheless, the year-to-date average of 1,177 trucks per operating day as at 30 September 2026 was 15% higher than the average of 1,023 trucks per operating day for the year ended 31 December 2025."]},{"type":"p","children":["The main operational data for the Group’s coking (metallurgical) coal ope